#set page(paper: "a4", margin: (x: 25mm, y: 22mm), fill: rgb("#f9f6f0"))
#set text(font: "Libertinus Serif", size: 12pt, fill: rgb("#3a3330"))
#set par(leading: 0.8em)
#let rust = rgb("#a4553e")
#let muted = rgb("#8a7970")
#align(center)[
  #text(font: "DejaVu Sans Mono", size: 8pt, tracking: 0.14em, fill: rust)[A LETTER FROM THE STUDIO]
  #v(4mm)
  #line(length: 28mm, stroke: 1pt + rust)
]
#v(17mm)
#align(right)[#text(size: 10pt, fill: muted)[Portland, 18 May 2026]]
#v(12mm)
Dear friend,

There is something wonderful about making space for a new idea. It begins as a
small observation, gathers shape through conversation, and becomes more real
each time someone gives it their attention.

This little note is an invitation to keep making things with care. Work slowly
enough to notice the details, generously enough to welcome other perspectives,
and boldly enough to try something you have not tried before.

#v(4mm)
#block(width: 100%, inset: (left: 8mm, y: 3mm), stroke: (left: 2pt + rust))[
  #text(size: 17pt, style: "italic", fill: rust)[The best ideas leave room for people.]
]
#v(4mm)
Thank you for being part of the story. We hope the next chapter brings you
curiosity, good company, and plenty of room to create.

#v(10mm)
Warmly, #linebreak()
#text(size: 18pt, style: "italic", fill: rust)[The Studio]
#v(1fr)
#align(center)[#text(font: "DejaVu Sans Mono", size: 8pt, fill: muted)[MADE WITH CARE  •  A FICTIONAL LETTER]]
